From 0a2cc9ee62c38d4aa7292ad872e036e225cf7f60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johnny Collado <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:40:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] IOP kernel: thmsgbx message boxes

The IOP interpreter had no thmsgbx, so IRX modules that use message boxes stopped at
their first call ("unhandled import thmsgbx:4"). Biohazard Outbreak's sound driver
creates one at start-up; without it the driver never registered its RPC server and
the game retried SdrBind forever.

CreateMbx, DeleteMbx, SendMbx, iSendMbx, ReceiveMbx, PollMbx, ReferMbxStatus and
iReferMbxStatus (ordinals 4-9, 11, 12, as in ps2sdk's thmsgbx). FIFO or priority
order for messages (MBA_MSPRI) and waiting threads (MBA_THPRI); KE_MBOX_NOMSG,
KE_UNKNOWN_MBXID, KE_ILLEGAL_ATTR and KE_WAIT_DELETE as on hardware. The queue is
kept in the kernel; the guest messages' next fields are not written.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
